   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1b59900c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Similarity matching for Models, Transmission and fuel columns (Fuzzy Match)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 96,
   "id": "45edbd9d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "models = [\"golf\", \"veloste\", \"caddy\", \"yaris\", \"q2\", \"fiesta\", \"2 series\", \"3 series\", \"a3\", \"octavia\", \"passat\", \"focus\", \"insignia\", \"a class\", \"q3\", \"fabia\", \"ka+\", \"glc class\", \"i30\", \"c class\", \"polo\", \"e class\", \"q5\", \"up\", \"c-hr\", \"mokka x\", \"corsa\", \"astra\", \"tt\", \"5 series\", \"aygo\", \"4 series\", \"slk\", \"viva\", \"t-roc\", \"ecosport\", \"tucson\", \"x-class\", \"cl class\", \"ix20\", \"i20\", \"rapid\", \"a1\", \"auris\", \"sharan\", \"adam\", \"x3\", \"a8\", \"gls class\", \"b-max\", \"a4\", \"kona\", \"i10\", \"mokka\", \"s-max\", \"x2\", \"crossland x\", \"tiguan\", \"a5\", \"gle class\", \"zafira\", \"ioniq\", \"a6\", \"mondeo\", \"yeti outdoor\", \"x1\", \"scala\", \"s class\", \"1 series\", \"kamiq\", \"kuga\", \"tourneo connect\", \"q7\", \"gla class\", \"arteon\", \"sl class\", \"santa fe\", \"grandland x\", \"i800\", \"rav4\", \"touran\", \"citigo\", \"roomster\", \"prius\", \"corolla\", \"b class\", \"kodiaq\", \"v class\", \"caddy maxi life\", \"superb\", \"getz\", \"combo life\", \"beetle\", \"galaxy\", \"m3\", \"gtc\", \"x4\", \"ka\", \"ix35\", \"grand tourneo connect\", \"m4\", \"tourneo custom\", \"z4\", \"x5\", \"meriva\", \"rs6\", \"verso\", \"touareg\", \"shuttle\", \"cls class\", \"c-max\", \"puma\", \"cla class\", \"i40\", \"tiguan allspace\", \"6 series\", \"caravelle\", \"karoq\", \"i3\", \"grand c-max\", \"t-cross\", \"a7\", \"golf sv\", \"agila\", \"gt86\", \"yeti\", \"california\", \"land cruiser\", \"edge\", \"x6\", \"caddy life\", \"8 series\", \"fusion\", \"gl class\", \"scirocco\", \"z3\", \"proace verso\", \"hilux\", \"amarok\", \"cc\", \"7 series\", \"avensis\", \"eos\", \"m class\", \"grandland\", \"zafira tourer\", \"rs5\", \"r8\", \"mustang\", \"antara\", \"q8\", \"camry\", \"clk\", \"rs3\", \"jetta\", \"kadjar\", \"sq5\", \"rs4\", \"supra\", \"i8\", \"x7\", \"sq7\", \"g class\", \"s3\", \"crossland\", \"tigra\", \"escort\", \"glb class\", \"vivaro\", \"verso-s\", \"m5\", \"s4\", \"iq\", \"a2\", \"caddy maxi\", \"streetka\", \"cascada\", \"accent\", \"s8\", \"rs\", \"golf s\", \"ranger\", \"vectra\", \"ampera\", \"fox\", \"urban cruiser\", \"m2\", \"clc class\", \"m6\", \"s5\", \"terracan\", \"200\", \"220\", \"230\", \"NaN\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "short_models = [models[i] for i in range(len(models)) if len(models[i]) == 2]\n",
    "short_models = list(set(short_models)) # get unique short model names as a list\n",
    "\n",
    "transmission_types = [\"semi-auto\", \"manual\", \"automatic\", \"unkown\", \"NaN\", \"other\"]\n",
    "fuel_types = [\"petrol\", \"diesel\", \"hybrid\", \"electric\", \"other\", \"NaN\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 97,
   "id": "a24b79fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Source for process.extractOne (fuzzy): https://github.com/seatgeek/thefuzz\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(len(df)): \n",
    "    if len(df.model[i]) > 2: # Only perform fuzzy matching for models that have a name longer than 2 letters -> fuzzy will become fuzzy (unreliable) if names are to short\n",
    "        df.loc[i, \"model\"] = process.extractOne(df.model[i], models)[0] # [0] because we get the name and score as a return -> score used for debugging\n",
    "    elif len(df.model[i]) == 2: # Use the short names list for comparisons if the model names are 2 letters\n",
    "        df.loc[i, \"model\"] = process.extractOne(df.model[i], short_models)[0]\n",
    "    else: # We can define models with only one letter\n",
    "        df.loc[i, \"model\"] = \"NaN\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    df.loc[i, \"transmission\"] = process.extractOne(df.transmission[i], transmission_types)[0]\n",
    "    df.loc[i, \"fuelType\"] = process.extractOne(df.fuelType[i], fuel_types)[0]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 98,
   "id": "599d1ea3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert the str NaN values back to pd.NA for easier further processing and readability\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"model\"] = df[\"model\"].replace(\"NaN\", pd.NA)\n",
    "df[\"transmission\"] = df[\"transmission\"].replace([\"unkown\", \"NaN\", \"other\"], pd.NA)\n",
    "df[\"fuelType\"] = df[\"fuelType\"].replace([\"other\", \"NaN\"], pd.NA)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e77b6252",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Interpolate missing Brand names"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 99,
   "id": "5fe8df4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "brand_models = df.groupby(\"model\")[\"Brand\"].agg(lambda x: x.mode()) # Get the most frequent brand for each model -> returns df with model and brand\n",
    "df = pd.merge(df, brand_models, on=\"model\") # add the model and brand df to our main df (onyl add the brand columns, join on model)\n",
    "\n",
    "df.drop('Brand_x', axis=1, inplace=True) # remove the old brand column\n",
    "df = df.rename(columns={\"Brand_y\": \"Brand\"}) # rename new column\n",
    "cols = ['carID', 'Brand', 'model', 'year', 'price', 'transmission', 'mileage', 'fuelType', 'tax', 'mpg', 'engineSize', 'paintQuality%', 'previousOwners', 'hasDamage'] # rearange column order\n",
    "df = df[cols]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "655d4d7f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Interpolate missing transimission names\n",
    "Five of the car models in our dataset where only produced with one transmission type but contained missing values in our dataset. For these models we can fill in the missing values as we know which transmission type it should be. This fixes the NA for 140 values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 100,
   "id": "dcd0c2ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#transmission_models = df.groupby(\"model\")[\"transmission\"].unique() #.agg(lambda x: x.mode())\n",
    "\n",
    "\"\"\"adam: manual\n",
    "camry: automatic \n",
    "ka: manual\n",
    "m6: semi-auto\n",
    "puma: manual\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df.loc[df[\"model\"]== \"adam\", \"transmission\"] = \"manual\"\n",
    "df.loc[df[\"model\"]== \"camry\", \"transmission\"] = \"automatic\"\n",
    "df.loc[df[\"model\"]== \"ka\", \"transmission\"] = \"manual\"\n",
    "df.loc[df[\"model\"]== \"m6\", \"transmission\"] = \"semi-auto\"\n",
    "df.loc[df[\"model\"]== \"puma\", \"transmission\"] = \"manual\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f1c198f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cleaning numeric columns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 101,
   "id": "5c783f37",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.year = df.year.round(0)\n",
    "df.year =  pd.to_datetime(df[\"year\"])\n",
    "df.price = df.price.round(0) # Only integer prices, shouldn't change much\n",
    "df.mileage = abs(df.mileage.round(0))\n",
    "df.tax = abs(df.tax).round(0) # Turn negative values into positve\n",
    "df.mpg = abs(df.mpg.round(1)) # Leave one after comma digit\n",
    "df.previousOwners = abs(df.previousOwners.round())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "96e30aaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Removing unecessary comma digits\n",
    "For most of the numerical columns we have entries with unnecessary after comma numbers. For example 2011.2108... we remove those after additional digits as we assume they are caused by errors and not important information. \n",
    "We do the same for negative values, if present. As we believe those are created by typos or system failures (e.g. taxes entered as negative number could mean the employee thought a negative number is required because taxes are deducted)"
   ]
  },
